        "original_id": "02c11d84-9310-5af5-a0b3-8e4afb2e6397",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jessica Stroup, Scott Buck\n- TV series: Iron Fist, 90210, The Following, The Defenders\n- Films: Prom Night, Vampire Bats, Left in Darkness, The Hills Have Eyes 2\n- Franchises and concepts: Marvel Comics, Marvel Cinematic Universe, Netflix\n\nFacts:\n- Jessica Stroup was born on October 23, 1986, and she is an American actress.\n- Jessica Stroup is best known for playing Erin Silver on 90210, Max Hardy on The Following, and Joy Meachum in Iron Fist.\n- Jessica Stroup is regarded as a scream queen for starring in the horror films Prom Night, Vampire Bats, Left in Darkness, and The Hills Have Eyes 2.\n- Iron Fist is an American web television series created for Netflix by Scott Buck and based on the Marvel Comics character Iron Fist.\n- Iron Fist is set in the Marvel Cinematic Universe and shares continuity with the films of that franchise.\n- Iron Fist is the fourth in a series of shows that lead to The Defenders crossover miniseries.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "26e96de2-3e11-5fc1-8a6f-05f2b0258567",
        "text": "Page: Jessica Stroup. Sentence: Jessica Leigh Stroup (born October 23, 1986) is an American actress, best known for her role as Erin Silver on \"90210\", Max Hardy on \"The Following\", and Joy Meachum in \"Iron Fist\".\nPage: Jessica Stroup. Sentence: She is regarded as a scream queen for starring in the horror films \"Prom Night\", \"Vampire Bats\", \"Left in Darkness\", and \"The Hills Have Eyes 2\".\nPage: Iron Fist (TV series). Sentence: Marvel's Iron Fist, or simply Iron Fist, is an American web television series created for Netflix by Scott Buck, based on the Marvel Comics character of the same name.\nPage: Iron Fist (TV series). Sentence: It is set in the Marvel Cinematic Universe (MCU), sharing continuity with the films of the franchise and is the fourth in a series of shows that lead to \"The Defenders\" crossover miniseries.",
